From: Catalyst Linux
Subject: [PATCH] cardputerzero-audio: the jack's settings only once the card is up

At card probe, and at the jack's first report while the card is still
being bound, the codec's controls do not exist yet, so each setting failed
with -ENOENT ("failed to set IF DACL Mixer DACR DACL Mixer=on: -2") before
the sync work applied them properly. They are now applied only once the
card is instantiated (by the sync work, and by every jack change after),
and a line says when they have all landed: "speaker: 2 settings applied".

--- a/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-audio.c	2026-11-21 17:53:43.660044752 -0800
+++ b/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-audio.c	2026-11-21 17:54:58.819036275 -0800
@@ -216,9 +216,18 @@
 	struct device *dev = simple_priv_to_dev(&cz->simple);
 	struct cardputerzero_control_setting *settings;
 	unsigned int num_settings;
+	unsigned int failed = 0;
 	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Catalyst Linux: before the card is up the codec's controls do not
+	 * exist yet (each would fail with -ENOENT): the sync work applies them
+	 * once it is.
+	 */
+	if (!snd_soc_card_is_instantiated(card))
+		return;
+
 	if (hp_inserted) {
 		settings = cz->hp_present_controls;
 		num_settings = cz->num_hp_present_controls;
@@ -230,10 +239,15 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < num_settings; i++) {
 		ret = cardputerzero_set_enum_control(card, settings[i].control,
 						     settings[i].value);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
 			dev_warn(dev, "failed to set %s=%s: %d\n",
 				 settings[i].control, settings[i].value, ret);
+			failed++;
+		}
 	}
+	if (num_settings && !failed)
+		dev_info(dev, "%s: %u settings applied\n",
+			 hp_inserted ? "headphones" : "speaker", num_settings);
 }
 
 #define CARDPUTERZERO_SYNC_EVERY_MS	200
